  "evidencia": "Page: David I. Arkin. Sentence: David I. Arkin (December 19, 1906 – October 8, 1980) was an American teacher, painter, writer, and lyricist, and is the father of actor Alan Arkin.\nPage: Alan Arkin. Sentence: Alan Wolf Arkin (born March 26, 1934) is an American actor, director, screenwriter, musician, and singer.\nPage: Alan Arkin. Sentence: With a film career spanning more than 55 years, Arkin is known for his performances in \"Popi\"; \"Wait Until Dark\"; \"The Russians Are Coming, the Russians Are Coming\"; \"The Heart Is a Lonely Hunter\"; \"Catch-22\"; \"The In-Laws\"; \"Edward Scissorhands\"; \"Glengarry Glen Ross\"; \"Thirteen Conversations About One Thing\"; \"Little Miss Sunshine\"; and \"Argo\".\nPage: Black and White (Three Dog Night song). Sentence: \"Black and White\" is a song written in 1954 by David I. Arkin and Earl Robinson.",
