        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David I. Arkin, Alan Arkin, Earl Robinson\n- Works: “Black and White”\n- Topics: family relationship, careers, film performances\n\nFacts:\n- David I. Arkin was born on December 19, 1906, and died on October 8, 1980.\n- In 1954, David I. Arkin and Earl Robinson wrote the song “Black and White.”\n- David I. Arkin was an American teacher, painter, writer, and lyricist.\n- David I. Arkin was the father of actor Alan Arkin.\n- Alan Wolf Arkin was born on March 26, 1934.\n- Alan Arkin is an American actor, director, screenwriter, musician, and singer.\n- Alan Arkin had a film career spanning more than 55 years.\n- Alan Arkin is known for performances in “Popi,” “Wait Until Dark,” “The Russians Are Coming, the Russians Are Coming,” “The Heart Is a Lonely Hunter,” “Catch-22,” “The In-Laws,” “Edward Scissorhands,” “Glengarry Glen Ross,” “Thirteen Conversations About One Thing,” “Little Miss Sunshine,” and “Argo.”",
